  "question": {
    "text": "In an LC oscillator, if values of inductance and capacitance become twice and eight times, respectively, then the resonant frequency of oscillator becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> times its initial resonant frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resonance frequency of an LC oscillations circuit is stated as&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;represents inductance and capacitance of circuit.</p><p>Now, when inductance and capacitance changes, i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Then, resonant frequency is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>"
  }
}